      "text": "To find the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in the equation of the line \\(y = ax + b\\), we start by using the given points \\((4, 5)\\) and \\((8, 17)\\).\n\nFirst, we substitute the coordinates of the point \\((4, 5)\\) into the equation \\(y = ax + b\\):\n\\[\n5 = 4a + b\n\\]\nThis gives us the first equation:\n\\[\n4a + b = 5 \\quad \\text{(1)}\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinates of the point \\((8, 17)\\) into the equation \\(y = ax + b\\):\n\\[\n17 = 8a + b\n\\]\nThis gives us the second equation:\n\\[\n8a + b = 17 \\quad \\text{(2)}\n\\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4a + b = 5 \\\\\n8a + b = 17\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nTo eliminate \\(b\\), we subtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[\n(8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n4a = 12\n\\]\nSolving for \\(a\\), we get:\n\\[\na = 3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(a = 3\\), we substitute this value back into the first equation to solve for \\(b\\):\n\\[\n4(3) + b = 5\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n12 + b = 5\n\\]\nSolving for \\(b\\), we get:\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12 = -7\n\\]\n\nWe have found that \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -7\\). Therefore, the value of \\(a - b\\) is:\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
