      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(a - b\\) for the line \\(y = ax + b\\) that passes through the points \\((4, 5)\\) and \\((8, 17)\\), we first need to determine the slope \\(a\\) and the y-intercept \\(b\\).\n\nThe slope \\(a\\) of the line passing through two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is given by:\n\\[\na = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\n\\]\nSubstituting the given points \\((4, 5)\\) and \\((8, 17)\\) into the formula, we get:\n\\[\na = \\frac{17 - 5}{8 - 4} = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\n\\]\nSo, the slope \\(a\\) is 3. Now we can write the equation of the line as:\n\\[\ny = 3x + b\n\\]\nNext, we use one of the given points to find the y-intercept \\(b\\). Let's use the point \\((4, 5)\\):\n\\[\n5 = 3(4) + b\n\\]\nSimplifying the right side, we get:\n\\[\n5 = 12 + b\n\\]\nTo solve for \\(b\\), we subtract 12 from both sides:\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12 = -7\n\\]\nSo, the y-intercept \\(b\\) is \\(-7\\). Now we have the equation of the line:\n\\[\ny = 3x - 7\n\\]\nWe need to find the value of \\(a - b\\):\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\(a - b\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
