      "text": "To determine the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) for the line \\(y = ax + b\\) that passes through the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\), we start by using the point-slope form of the equation of a line. First, we find the slope \\(a\\):\n\nThe slope \\(a\\) is given by the formula:\n\\[\na = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\n\\]\nSubstituting the coordinates of the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\), we get:\n\\[\na = \\frac{17 - 5}{8 - 4} = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\n\\]\nSo, the slope \\(a\\) is 3. Now we substitute \\(a = 3\\) and the point \\((4,5)\\) into the line equation \\(y = ax + b\\) to find \\(b\\):\n\\[\n5 = 3 \\cdot 4 + b\n\\]\nSimplifying the right side, we get:\n\\[\n5 = 12 + b\n\\]\nSolving for \\(b\\), we subtract 12 from both sides:\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12 = -7\n\\]\nNow we have the equation of the line as:\n\\[\ny = 3x - 7\n\\]\nTo find \\(a - b\\), we substitute \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -7\\):\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\(a - b\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
